=== 3. JDBC Smoke Test Preconditions (PostgreSqlConnectionSmokeTest.java) ===
PostgreSqlConnectionSmokeTest.java SHA-256: 0e5b5e6a9ee980684f2d6006e081609f61f5a7dadaa07a52c61fa7bf28d06e48
application-postgresql.properties SHA-256: 0b39943ce2b84228eb0e94eff5ccd3ac35fd80e1d3a5af394fbdd9dd9d14e6f4
- Required env vars when enabled:
  1. SASMS_PG_SMOKE_ENABLED=true (otherwise JUnit assumeTrue skips test cleanly)
  2. SASMS_DB_URL=jdbc:postgresql://127.0.0.1:5432/sasms (restricted to loopback host, port 5432, path /sasms)
  3. SASMS_DB_USERNAME=<runtime_login_in_sasms_app> (must NOT be sasms_owner per Decision C2 / D54 section 4)
  4. SASMS_DB_PASSWORD=<secret> (never hardcoded)
- Compatibility of a login inheriting sasms_app with smoke test queries:
  * connection.setReadOnly(true) & SHOW transaction_read_only -> 'on' (SUPPORTED)
  * SHOW server_version -> '16.x' (SUPPORTED)
  * SELECT current_database() -> 'sasms' (SUPPORTED)
  * SELECT count(*) FROM information_schema.tables WHERE table_schema='sasms' AND table_type='BASE TABLE' -> 37 (SUPPORTED because sasms_app has SELECT ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA sasms)
  * SELECT count(*) FROM sasms.roles -> 9 (SUPPORTED)
  * SELECT count(*) FROM sasms.products -> 2 (SUPPORTED)
  * connection.rollback() -> clean read-only rollback (SUPPORTED)

